<div class="space-y-10">
  <section>
    <h3>Meaningful inline SVG icons</h3>
    <p>These examples use the same search icon. The first two expose the name “Search.” The last one is meaningful but unnamed.</p>
    <div class="icon-example-grid" aria-label="Meaningful SVG icon examples">
      <figure class="icon-example">
        <div class="icon-example__demo">
          <svg role="img" aria-labelledby="svg-title-search" class="demo-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
            <title id="svg-title-search">Search</title>
            <circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.25" />
            <path d="M15.5 15.5L21 21" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-width="2.25" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <figcaption><strong>Accessible:</strong> inline SVG with <code>&lt;title&gt;</code> and <code>aria-labelledby</code>.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="icon-example">
        <div class="icon-example__demo">
          <svg role="img" aria-label="Search" class="demo-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
            <circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.25" />
            <path d="M15.5 15.5L21 21" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-width="2.25" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <figcaption><strong>Accessible:</strong> inline SVG with <code>role="img"</code> and <code>aria-label</code>.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="icon-example icon-example--warning">
        <div class="icon-example__demo">
          <svg class="demo-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
            <circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.25" />
            <path d="M15.5 15.5L21 21" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-width="2.25" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <figcaption><strong>Not accessible:</strong> meaningful SVG with no accessible name.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h3>Decorative inline SVG icons</h3>
    <p>When visible text already explains a control, its icon is usually decorative and should not add another announcement.</p>
    <div class="icon-example-grid" aria-label="Decorative SVG icon examples">
      <figure class="icon-example">
        <div class="icon-example__demo">
          <button type="button" class="icon-button-demo">
            <svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" class="button-demo-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
              <path d="M5 12H19" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-width="2.25" />
              <path d="M13 6L19 12L13 18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2.25" />
            </svg>
            Continue
          </button>
        </div>
        <figcaption><strong>Accessible:</strong> the button text supplies the name and the SVG is hidden.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="icon-example icon-example--warning">
        <div class="icon-example__demo">
          <button type="button" class="icon-button-demo">
            <svg role="img" aria-label="Arrow" class="button-demo-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
              <path d="M5 12H19" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-width="2.25" />
              <path d="M13 6L19 12L13 18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2.25" />
            </svg>
            Continue
          </button>
        </div>
        <figcaption><strong>Not ideal:</strong> the decorative icon may add “Arrow” to the announcement.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h3>CSS-generated icons</h3>
    <p>Generated content can be exposed differently by different browser and screen-reader combinations. Listen to each pattern rather than assuming support.</p>
    <div class="icon-example-grid" aria-label="CSS generated icon examples">
      <figure class="icon-example">
        <div class="icon-example__demo"><span class="css-icon css-icon--circle">Profile status</span></div>
        <figcaption><strong>Accessible:</strong> visible text provides the name and the circle is decorative.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="icon-example icon-example--warning">
        <div class="icon-example__demo"><div class="css-icon css-icon--arrow-only" role="img" aria-label="Next step"></div></div>
        <figcaption><strong>ARIA name:</strong> the otherwise textless visual is named “Next step.”</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="icon-example icon-example--warning">
        <div class="icon-example__demo"><span class="css-icon css-icon--arrow-empty"></span></div>
        <figcaption><strong>Not accessible:</strong> the visual arrow has no accessible name.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="icon-example">
        <div class="icon-example__demo"><span class="css-icon css-icon--arrow-alt">Continue</span></div>
        <figcaption><strong>Generated alternative:</strong> <code>content: "→" / ""</code> can treat the arrow as decorative where supported.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<style>
  .icon-example-grid { display: grid; gap: 1rem; margin-block: 1.5rem 3rem; }
  .icon-example { border: 2px solid #bbc9f7; padding: 1rem; }
  :global(.dark) .icon-example { border-color: #18399a; }
  .icon-example--warning { border-style: dashed; }
  .icon-example__demo { align-items: center; display: flex; min-height: 4rem; }
  .demo-icon { color: #54007b; height: 3rem; width: 3rem; }
  :global(.dark) .demo-icon { color: #ade5f8; }
  .button-demo-icon { height: 1.5rem; width: 1.5rem; }
  .icon-button-demo { align-items: center; background-color: #033573; border: 4px solid transparent; color: white; display: inline-flex; gap: .5rem; padding: .75rem 1rem; }
  :global(.dark) .icon-button-demo { background-color: #ade5f8; color: black; }
  .icon-button-demo:hover { background-color: transparent; border-color: #033573; color: #033573; }
  :global(.dark) .icon-button-demo:hover { border-color: #ade5f8; color: #ade5f8; }
  .icon-button-demo:focus { outline: 2px solid black; outline-offset: 4px; }
  :global(.dark) .icon-button-demo:focus { outline-color: white; }
  .css-icon { align-items: center; display: inline-flex; gap: .5rem; }
  .css-icon--circle::before { background-color: #54007b; border-radius: 999px; content: ""; display: inline-block; height: 1rem; width: 1rem; }
  :global(.dark) .css-icon--circle::before { background-color: #ade5f8; }
  .css-icon--arrow-only::before, .css-icon--arrow-empty::before, .css-icon--arrow-alt::before { color: #54007b; font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1; }
  :global(.dark) .css-icon--arrow-only::before, :global(.dark) .css-icon--arrow-empty::before, :global(.dark) .css-icon--arrow-alt::before { color: #ade5f8; }
  .css-icon--arrow-only::before, .css-icon--arrow-empty::before { content: "→"; }
  .css-icon--arrow-alt::before { content: "→" / ""; }
  @media (min-width: 48rem) { .icon-example-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
</style>
